{"uncertainty": 0.27, "outcome": "Delivered two files for the four-requester round-robin arbiter: the RTL (rr_arbiter.v, top rr_arbiter) and a self-checking testbench (rr_arbiter_tb.v, top rr_arbiter_tb). No lint, simulation, synthesis or formal run was done by this seat. The required tool runs and the independent review are still to be recorded.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "design_note", "title": "rr_arbiter implementation decisions and deviations", "summary": "Traceable to [requirement:req-142be1ce31], built from [artifact:prj-1b70baad63.microarchitecture.a1] and [artifact:prj-1b70baad63.interface-spec.a1].\n\nState matches microarchitecture section 1: one $clog2(N)-bit pointer, reset synchronously to 0.\n\nRecorded deviation, grant search (section 2): the spec describes one walk from ptr that wraps at LAST. The RTL instead searches in two passes over fixed indices. Pass 1 picks the lowest index at or above ptr with req high. If there is none, pass 2 picks the lowest index with req high. This chooses the same winner as the wrapping walk, and section 2 itself says a masked priority encoder has the same behavior. It was chosen so every bit-select uses a loop index that unrolls to a constant, and every comparison and increment has matched widths (needed to be clean under -Wall with no waivers).\n\nWrap handling: the pointer still wraps by comparing with LAST (N-1), not at a power of two.\n\nGrant is combinational from req and ptr and is not gated by reset (interface spec section 5)."}], "files": [{"path": "rr_arbiter.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "rr_arbiter RTL (parameter N, default 4)", "summary": "Synthesizable Verilog for the round-robin arbiter required by [requirement:req-142be1ce31].\n\nPorts and parameter follow [artifact:prj-1b70baad63.interface-spec.a1]: clk, rst_n (active low, synchronous), req[N-1:0], grant[N-1:0], and parameter N.\n\nStructure follows [artifact:prj-1b70baad63.microarchitecture.a1]:\n- the pointer is the only state;\n- the combinational grant logic gives every output a default first, so there is no latch;\n- on a cycle with a grant, the pointer moves to one past the winner, wrapping at N-1; otherwise it holds.\n\nDesign-intent assertions sit under `ifdef FORMAL`:\n- the pointer is in range and is 0 after reset;\n- the grant is one-hot or zero, only to a requester, and work conserving;\n- no requester with req high lies between the pointer and the winner;\n- the pointer update rule holds;\n- each requester waits at most N-1 cycles, with the induction invariant wait plus distance <= N-1.\n\nThese assertions are not proven: no formal_spec is submitted. The RTL never calls $finish or $stop and reads no plusargs.", "entry": "rr_arbiter"}, {"path": "rr_arbiter_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking testbench, N 4 and N 5 side by side", "summary": "Implements the verification requirements of [artifact:prj-1b70baad63.interface-spec.a1] section 6 and the plan in [artifact:prj-1b70baad63.microarchitecture.a1] section 5.\n\nTwo arbiters run together, at N=4 and N=5. In every cycle the testbench:\n- checks each grant against a reference pointer model;\n- keeps a wait counter per requester and fails if any held request waits N cycles.\n\nDirected phases cover: reset, no requests, each requester alone, strict rotation 0..N-1 after reset, a held request among changing others, and reset during traffic with the pointer away from 0. The longest fair wait of N-1 cycles is reached during the rotation phase. A random phase follows, with contention and occasional resets.\n\nCoverage counters fail the run if any case was not reached. Every failure goes through $error, and passing checks are counted. The verdict line is printed once, just before $finish: NIRMAAN-SIM <nonce> <passed> passed, <failed> failed, with the nonce read via $value$plusargs into reg [8*64-1:0].", "entry": "rr_arbiter_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["No lint, simulation, synthesis, formal or cover run was performed by this seat. Whether the files are lint-clean, pass simulation and synthesize without latches is unverified until the platform's runs are recorded.", "The FORMAL block in rr_arbiter.v is unproven design intent. No formal_spec (.sby) file was submitted because the expected outputs are rtl_source and testbench only.", "The microarchitecture verification plan's rr_arbiter_tb_fail.v (failure-path run) and the rr_arbiter.sby / rr_arbiter_n5.sby proofs are not produced here. They remain open against the interface spec section 6 formal requirement.", "The two-pass masked search is claimed to choose the same winner as the wrapping walk in microarchitecture section 2. This equivalence is argued, not checked by a tool.", "Both files use `timescale 1ns / 1ps so Verilator does not raise TIMESCALEMOD when they are compiled together. The testbench uses # delays, so Verilator needs --timing. $error requires SystemVerilog mode under Icarus.", "The design assumes N >= 2, per interface spec section 1. With N = 1, $clog2(N) = 0 and the pointer width would be invalid."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Seat: design.rtl.design.interconnect.senior. For review by an independent reviewer, not the author (P6). Reviewers should check the recorded grant-search deviation and the open formal and fail-path items. The deviation keeps the specified behavior; the formal and fail-path items need a decision on whether a separate formal_spec task will cover the interface spec's formal proof requirement."}

=== FILE: rr_arbiter.v ===
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
`default_nettype none

// rr_arbiter: round-robin arbiter for N requesters (default 4).
// Implements interface_spec.md / microarchitecture.md for rr_arbiter.
//
// * One state register, ptr ($clog2(N) bits): the requester with the highest
//   priority this cycle. Reset (synchronous, active low) sets it to 0.
// * grant is combinational from req and ptr: the winner is the first
//   requester with req high at or after ptr, wrapping from N-1 to 0.
//   The search is done as two passes over constant indices (at/above ptr,
//   then from 0), which selects the same winner as a wrapping walk.
// * On a rising edge with a grant, ptr moves to one past the winner,
//   wrapping by comparison with LAST (N-1), so N need not be a power of two.
//   With no request, ptr holds. grant is not gated by reset.

module rr_arbiter #(
    parameter integer N = 4
) (
    input  wire         clk,
    input  wire         rst_n,
    input  wire [N-1:0] req,
    output reg  [N-1:0] grant
);

    localparam integer  PW     = $clog2(N);
    localparam integer  LAST_I = N - 1;
    localparam integer  ONE_I  = 1;
    localparam [PW-1:0] LAST   = LAST_I[PW-1:0];
    localparam [PW-1:0] ONE    = ONE_I[PW-1:0];

    reg [PW-1:0] ptr;
    reg [PW-1:0] ptr_nxt;
    reg [PW-1:0] cand;
    reg          found;
    integer      j;

    // Grant logic and next pointer. Every output has a default first.
    always @(*) begin
        grant   = {N{1'b0}};
        ptr_nxt = ptr;
        found   = 1'b0;
        cand    = {PW{1'b0}};
        // Pass 1: requesters at or above the pointer.
        for (j = 0; j < N; j = j + 1) begin
            if (!found && req[j] && (cand >= ptr)) begin
                found    = 1'b1;
                grant[j] = 1'b1;
                ptr_nxt  = (cand == LAST) ? {PW{1'b0}} : (cand + ONE);
            end
            cand = cand + ONE;
        end
        // Pass 2: wrap around, requesters below the pointer.
        cand = {PW{1'b0}};
        for (j = 0; j < N; j = j + 1) begin
            if (!found && req[j]) begin
                found    = 1'b1;
                grant[j] = 1'b1;
                ptr_nxt  = (cand == LAST) ? {PW{1'b0}} : (cand + ONE);
            end
            cand = cand + ONE;
        end
    end

    // Pointer register: synchronous active-low reset to 0.
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (!rst_n) begin
            ptr <= {PW{1'b0}};
        end else begin
            ptr <= ptr_nxt;
        end
    end

`ifdef FORMAL
    // Design-intent properties (SymbiYosys, read with -formal -sv).
    reg f_past_valid;
    initial f_past_valid = 1'b0;
    always @(posedge clk) f_past_valid <= 1'b1;

    always @(*) if (!f_past_valid) assume (!rst_n);

    // Circular distance from pointer p to requester idx.
    function integer f_dist;
        input integer idx;
        input integer p;
        begin
            if (idx >= p) f_dist = idx - p;
            else          f_dist = idx + N - p;
        end
    endfunction

    integer f_k;
    integer f_j;
    integer f_ptr;
    integer f_win;

    always @(*) begin
        f_ptr = ptr;
        f_win = 0;
        for (f_k = 0; f_k < N; f_k = f_k + 1)
            if (grant[f_k]) f_win = f_k;
    end

    always @(*) begin
        assert ($onehot0(grant));
        assert ((grant & ~req) == {N{1'b0}});
        assert ((req == {N{1'b0}}) || (grant != {N{1'b0}}));
        if (f_past_valid) begin
            assert (ptr <= LAST);
            for (f_j = 0; f_j < N; f_j = f_j + 1)
                if ((grant != {N{1'b0}}) && (f_dist(f_j, f_ptr) < f_dist(f_win, f_ptr)))
                    assert (!req[f_j]);
        end
    end

    reg          f_rst_n_q;
    reg          f_any_q;
    reg [PW-1:0] f_win_q;
    reg [PW-1:0] f_ptr_q;
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        f_rst_n_q <= rst_n;
        f_any_q   <= |grant;
        f_win_q   <= f_win[PW-1:0];
        f_ptr_q   <= ptr;
    end

    always @(*) begin
        if (f_past_valid) begin
            if (!f_rst_n_q)
                assert (ptr == {PW{1'b0}});
            else if (f_any_q)
                assert (ptr == ((f_win_q == LAST) ? {PW{1'b0}} : (f_win_q + ONE)));
            else
                assert (ptr == f_ptr_q);
        end
    end

    // Fairness: cycles waited with the request held never exceed N-1.
    genvar f_g;
    generate
        for (f_g = 0; f_g < N; f_g = f_g + 1) begin : f_fair
            reg [7:0] f_wait;
            initial f_wait = 8'd0;
            always @(posedge clk) begin
                if (!rst_n || !req[f_g] || grant[f_g])
                    f_wait <= 8'd0;
                else if (f_wait != 8'hff)
                    f_wait <= f_wait + 8'd1;
            end
            always @(*) begin
                assert (f_wait <= LAST_I);
                if (f_past_valid && (f_wait != 8'd0))
                    assert ((f_wait + f_dist(f_g, f_ptr)) <= LAST_I);
            end
        end
    endgenerate
`endif

endmodule

`default_nettype wire
=== END FILE ===
=== FILE: rr_arbiter_tb.v ===
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
`default_nettype none

// Self-checking testbench for rr_arbiter.
// Two arbiters run side by side, N=4 and N=5 (not a power of two). Every
// cycle each grant is checked against a reference pointer model, and each
// requester's wait with its request held is checked against N-1. Coverage
// counters fail the run if a case from the interface spec was not reached.
// Ends with one verdict line just before $finish.

module rr_arbiter_tb;

    reg        clk;
    reg        rst_n;
    reg  [3:0] req4;
    reg  [4:0] req5;
    wire [3:0] grant4;
    wire [4:0] grant5;

    rr_arbiter #(.N(4)) dut4 (
        .clk   (clk),
        .rst_n (rst_n),
        .req   (req4),
        .grant (grant4)
    );

    rr_arbiter #(.N(5)) dut5 (
        .clk   (clk),
        .rst_n (rst_n),
        .req   (req5),
        .grant (grant5)
    );

    integer passed;
    integer failed;

    // Reference model state, index 0: N=4, index 1: N=5.
    integer   mptr   [0:1];
    integer   mnext  [0:1];
    integer   wt     [0:15];   // wait counters, base 0 (N=4) and 8 (N=5)
    reg [7:0] prev_r [0:1];

    // Coverage counters.
    integer cov_none  [0:1];
    integer cov_all   [0:1];
    integer cov_held  [0:1];
    integer cov_long  [0:1];
    integer cov_rst   [0:1];
    integer cov_alone [0:15];

    integer        rot_on;
    integer        rot_c;
    integer        i;
    integer        c;
    reg [31:0]     rnd;
    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;

    initial clk = 1'b0;
    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    // xorshift32 pseudo-random source.
    task next_rnd;
        begin
            rnd = rnd ^ (rnd << 13);
            rnd = rnd ^ (rnd >> 17);
            rnd = rnd ^ (rnd << 5);
        end
    endtask

    // Check one arbiter for the current cycle and compute its model's next pointer.
    task check_arb;
        input integer which;
        input integer n;
        input [7:0]   r;
        input [7:0]   g;
        integer   k;
        integer   idx;
        integer   base;
        integer   win;
        reg [7:0] expg;
        reg [7:0] allm;
        reg       done;
        begin
            base = which * 8;
            expg = 8'd0;
            allm = 8'd0;
            done = 1'b0;
            win  = 0;
            for (k = 0; k < n; k = k + 1) begin
                allm[k] = 1'b1;
                idx = mptr[which] + k;
                if (idx >= n) idx = idx - n;
                if (!done && r[idx]) begin
                    expg[idx] = 1'b1;
                    done      = 1'b1;
                    win       = idx;
                end
            end

            // Grant against the reference pointer model.
            if (g === expg) begin
                passed = passed + 1;
            end else begin
                failed = failed + 1;
                $error("N=%0d t=%0t req=%b grant=%b expected=%b model_ptr=%0d",
                       n, $time, r, g, expg, mptr[which]);
            end

            // Coverage.
            if (r == 8'd0) cov_none[which] = cov_none[which] + 1;
            if (r == allm) cov_all[which] = cov_all[which] + 1;
            for (k = 0; k < n; k = k + 1)
                if ((r == (8'd1 << k)) && g[k])
                    cov_alone[base + k] = cov_alone[base + k] + 1;
            if (!rst_n && (r != 8'd0) && (mptr[which] != 0))
                cov_rst[which] = cov_rst[which] + 1;

            // Fairness: no held request waits N cycles.
            for (k = 0; k < n; k = k + 1) begin
                if (r[k] && (wt[base + k] >= 1) &&
                    (((r ^ prev_r[which]) & ~(8'd1 << k)) != 8'd0))
                    cov_held[which] = cov_held[which] + 1;
                if (!rst_n || !r[k] || g[k]) begin
                    wt[base + k] = 0;
                end else begin
                    wt[base + k] = wt[base + k] + 1;
                    if (wt[base + k] > n - 1) begin
                        failed = failed + 1;
                        $error("N=%0d t=%0t requester %0d waited %0d cycles with req held",
                               n, $time, k, wt[base + k]);
                    end else begin
                        passed = passed + 1;
                    end
                    if (wt[base + k] == n - 1)
                        cov_long[which] = cov_long[which] + 1;
                end
            end
            prev_r[which] = r;

            // Model pointer for the next cycle.
            if (!rst_n)
                mnext[which] = 0;
            else if (done)
                mnext[which] = (win == n - 1) ? 0 : win + 1;
            else
                mnext[which] = mptr[which];
        end
    endtask

    // One cycle: inputs were set at posedge+1; check at posedge+3; advance.
    task tick;
        begin
            #2;
            check_arb(0, 4, {4'b0000, req4}, {4'b0000, grant4});
            check_arb(1, 5, {3'b000, req5}, {3'b000, grant5});
            if (rot_on != 0) begin
                if (grant4 === (4'd1 << (rot_c % 4))) begin
                    passed = passed + 1;
                end else begin
                    failed = failed + 1;
                    $error("rotation N=4 step %0d: grant=%b, expected requester %0d",
                           rot_c, grant4, rot_c % 4);
                end
                if (grant5 === (5'd1 << (rot_c % 5))) begin
                    passed = passed + 1;
                end else begin
                    failed = failed + 1;
                    $error("rotation N=5 step %0d: grant=%b, expected requester %0d",
                           rot_c, grant5, rot_c % 5);
                end
                rot_c = rot_c + 1;
            end
            @(posedge clk);
            #1;
            mptr[0] = mnext[0];
            mptr[1] = mnext[1];
        end
    endtask

    task cover_item;
        input integer n;
        input integer item;
        input integer k;
        input integer count;
        begin
            if (count > 0) begin
                passed = passed + 1;
            end else begin
                failed = failed + 1;
                case (item)
                    0: $error("coverage N=%0d: no cycle without requests", n);
                    1: $error("coverage N=%0d: no cycle with every requester requesting", n);
                    2: $error("coverage N=%0d: no held request among changing others", n);
                    3: $error("coverage N=%0d: longest fair wait (N-1) never reached", n);
                    4: $error("coverage N=%0d: no reset during traffic", n);
                    5: $error("coverage N=%0d: requester %0d never granted alone", n, k);
                    default: $error("coverage N=%0d: unknown item %0d", n, item);
                endcase
            end
        end
    endtask

    initial begin
        passed = 0;
        failed = 0;
        for (i = 0; i < 2; i = i + 1) begin
            mptr[i]     = 0;
            mnext[i]    = 0;
            prev_r[i]   = 8'd0;
            cov_none[i] = 0;
            cov_all[i]  = 0;
            cov_held[i] = 0;
            cov_long[i] = 0;
            cov_rst[i]  = 0;
        end
        for (i = 0; i < 16; i = i + 1) begin
            wt[i]        = 0;
            cov_alone[i] = 0;
        end
        rot_on = 0;
        rot_c  = 0;
        rnd    = 32'h1234_5678;
        nonce  = {(8*64){1'b0}};

        // Reset with no traffic; checking starts after the first reset edge.
        rst_n = 1'b0;
        req4  = 4'd0;
        req5  = 5'd0;
        @(posedge clk);
        #1;
        mptr[0] = 0;
        mptr[1] = 0;
        tick;
        tick;
        rst_n = 1'b1;

        // No requests.
        for (c = 0; c < 3; c = c + 1) tick;

        // Each requester alone.
        for (i = 0; i < 5; i = i + 1) begin
            req4 = (i < 4) ? (4'd1 << i) : 4'd0;
            req5 = 5'd1 << i;
            tick;
            tick;
        end

        // Reset, then everyone requests: strict rotation from requester 0.
        // Every requester also waits the longest fair wait, N-1 cycles.
        req4  = 4'd0;
        req5  = 5'd0;
        rst_n = 1'b0;
        tick;
        rst_n  = 1'b1;
        req4   = 4'hF;
        req5   = 5'h1F;
        rot_on = 1;
        rot_c  = 0;
        for (c = 0; c < 20; c = c + 1) tick;
        rot_on = 0;

        // A held request (requester 2) among changing others.
        for (c = 0; c < 40; c = c + 1) begin
            next_rnd;
            req4 = rnd[3:0] | 4'b0100;
            req5 = rnd[8:4] | 5'b00100;
            tick;
        end

        // Reset during traffic, with both pointers away from 0.
        req4 = 4'hF;
        req5 = 5'h1F;
        tick;
        c = 0;
        while (((mptr[0] == 0) || (mptr[1] == 0)) && (c < 20)) begin
            tick;
            c = c + 1;
        end
        rst_n = 1'b0;
        tick;
        tick;
        rst_n  = 1'b1;
        rot_on = 1;
        rot_c  = 0;
        for (c = 0; c < 10; c = c + 1) tick;
        rot_on = 0;

        // Random contention with occasional resets.
        for (c = 0; c < 400; c = c + 1) begin
            next_rnd;
            req4  = rnd[3:0] | rnd[7:4];
            req5  = rnd[12:8] | rnd[17:13];
            rst_n = (rnd[24:20] != 5'd0);
            tick;
        end
        rst_n = 1'b1;
        req4  = 4'd0;
        req5  = 5'd0;
        tick;

        // Coverage: every case from the interface spec must have been reached.
        for (i = 0; i < 2; i = i + 1) begin
            cover_item(4 + i, 0, 0, cov_none[i]);
            cover_item(4 + i, 1, 0, cov_all[i]);
            cover_item(4 + i, 2, 0, cov_held[i]);
            cover_item(4 + i, 3, 0, cov_long[i]);
            cover_item(4 + i, 4, 0, cov_rst[i]);
            for (c = 0; c < 4 + i; c = c + 1)
                cover_item(4 + i, 5, c, cov_alone[i * 8 + c]);
        end

        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) nonce = {(8*64){1'b0}};
        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
        $finish;
    end

endmodule

`default_nettype wire
=== END FILE ===
